{"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/amplitudeencoding"]}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/AmplitudeEncoding\/documentation\/AmplitudeEncoding","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"sections":[],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Send records to an Amplitude project through its HTTP V2 API."}],"metadata":{"role":"collection","title":"AmplitudeEncoding","externalID":"AmplitudeEncoding","symbolKind":"module","modules":[{"name":"AmplitudeEncoding"}],"roleHeading":"Framework"},"kind":"symbol","topicSections":[{"anchor":"Sending-to-Amplitude","title":"Sending to Amplitude","identifiers":["doc:\/\/AmplitudeEncoding\/documentation\/AmplitudeEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/amplitude(apiKey:region:plan:backoff:clock:)","doc:\/\/AmplitudeEncoding\/documentation\/AmplitudeEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/amplitude(apiKey:region:plan:transport:backoff:clock:)","doc:\/\/AmplitudeEncoding\/documentation\/AmplitudeEncoding\/AmplitudeRegion","doc:\/\/AmplitudeEncoding\/documentation\/AmplitudeEncoding\/AmplitudeSetupError"]},{"anchor":"Encoding-batches","title":"Encoding batches","identifiers":["doc:\/\/AmplitudeEncoding\/documentation\/AmplitudeEncoding\/AmplitudeBatchEncoder"]},{"anchor":"Records-left-out","title":"Records left out","identifiers":["doc:\/\/AmplitudeEncoding\/documentation\/AmplitudeEncoding\/AmplitudeEncodingError"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/AmplitudeEncoding\/documentation\/AmplitudeEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/amplitude(apiKey:region:plan:backoff:clock:)","isActive":true},{"text":" makes an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"HTTPDestination","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (module ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations","isActive":true},{"text":") for your Amplitude project in one call. It checks","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the API key, posts to the HTTP V2 endpoint of the project’s data residency (","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/AmplitudeEncoding\/documentation\/AmplitudeEncoding\/AmplitudeRegion","isActive":true},{"text":")","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"with an ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/AmplitudeEncoding\/documentation\/AmplitudeEncoding\/AmplitudeBatchEncoder","isActive":true},{"text":", and splits each batch to Amplitude’s limits","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/AmplitudeEncoding\/documentation\/AmplitudeEncoding\/AmplitudeBatchEncoder\/batchLimit","isActive":true},{"text":"): 10 events and 1 MB a request, which a project on any plan","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"accepts. A batch with no record the encoder can write, an empty one included, makes no request. It","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"retries no response, a 5xx, 408 and 429, and drops and reports any other status. The API key goes","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"in the body, so no header field is needed, and no trace context is sent. ","type":"text"},{"code":"import Traffluent","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"leaves this module out; import it on its own.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The region has no default. A project’s data resides in Amplitude’s default data center or its EU"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one, and an event posted to the other doesn’t reach it, so you pick the region on purpose. The"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"factory throws "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/AmplitudeEncoding\/documentation\/AmplitudeEncoding\/AmplitudeSetupError"},{"type":"text","text":" for an empty key, and for an Amplitude Experiment deployment"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"key, which isn’t the project’s API key."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each record becomes an event of an anonymous device. Its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"device_id"},{"type":"text","text":" is the record’s session,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"from the sessions enricher, and its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"session_id"},{"type":"text","text":" that session’s start in Unix milliseconds; a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"record with no session is sent under its own record identifier, with no "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"session_id"},{"type":"text","text":". No "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"user_id"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is sent. Its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"insert_id"},{"type":"text","text":" is the record’s identifier, which a redelivered record keeps, and its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"time"},{"type":"text","text":" the record’s timestamp in epoch milliseconds. The record’s vendor identifier and trace"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"context aren’t sent, nor is an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ip"},{"type":"text","text":", and the standard context is sent as Amplitude’s own fields"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"app_version"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"device_model"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"language"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"platform"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"os_name"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"os_version"},{"type":"text","text":")."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Amplitude counts a user per ","type":"text"},{"code":"device_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and bills by monthly tracked users, so each session counts","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"as one tracked user, and so does each record sent without a session.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Properties are read through the event’s schema in the ","type":"text"},{"code":"TrackingPlan","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" the encoder is made with, into","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"event_properties","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". A ","type":"text"},{"code":"Sensitive","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" value is never sent, whatever the record reveals. A record the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"encoder can’t write is left out and the rest of the batch is sent: one the plan doesn’t describe,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"one whose event name Amplitude keeps for its own (","type":"text"},{"code":"[Amplitude] …","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"$identify","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"$groupidentify","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"),","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"one whose event isn’t ","type":"text"},{"code":"Encodable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", one holding a value JSON can’t, one whose timestamp has no","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"epoch-milliseconds form, and one too large for a request. The destination reports each as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"HTTPDropReport.skipped(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", a ","type":"text"},{"code":"SkippedRecord","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" whose reason is an ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/AmplitudeEncoding\/documentation\/AmplitudeEncoding\/AmplitudeEncodingError"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"To send to PostHog, use "},{"code":"PostHogEncoding","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" instead."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["import AmplitudeEncoding","import HTTPDestinations","import TrackingPlans","","let plan = try TrackingPlan()","let amplitude = try HTTPDestination.amplitude(","    apiKey: apiKey,","    region: .us,  \/\/ or .eu, where the project's data resides","    plan: plan)","let tracker = Tracker(enrichers: [.sessions()])","let delivery = tracker.records.batch().deliver(to: amplitude)"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The guide ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/choosingdestinations","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"covers what Amplitude receives, and why, in more detail.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"references":{"doc://AmplitudeEncoding/documentation/AmplitudeEncoding/AmplitudeEncodingError":{"kind":"symbol","title":"AmplitudeEncodingError","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/amplitudeencoding\/amplitudeencodingerror","identifier":"doc:\/\/AmplitudeEncoding\/documentation\/AmplitudeEncoding\/AmplitudeEncodingError","abstract":[{"text":"Why ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/AmplitudeEncoding\/documentation\/AmplitudeEncoding\/AmplitudeBatchEncoder"},{"text":" couldn’t send a record, which it leaves out of the batch’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"requests as a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SkippedRecord"},{"text":", and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"text":" reports as a drop. When it can encode no","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"record of a batch, it makes no request, and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"text":" sends nothing for the batch.","type":"text"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"AmplitudeEncodingError"}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"AmplitudeEncodingError"}]},"doc://AmplitudeEncoding/documentation/AmplitudeEncoding/AmplitudeBatchEncoder":{"title":"AmplitudeBatchEncoder","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"AmplitudeBatchEncoder","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/amplitudeencoding\/amplitudebatchencoder","abstract":[{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder","type":"reference"},{"text":" of Amplitude’s HTTP V2 API, so an ","type":"text"},{"code":"HTTPDestination","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" can","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"send events to an Amplitude project’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"POST \/2\/httpapi","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"AmplitudeBatchEncoder","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/AmplitudeEncoding\/documentation\/AmplitudeEncoding\/AmplitudeBatchEncoder"},"doc://AmplitudeEncoding/documentation/AmplitudeEncoding":{"title":"AmplitudeEncoding","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/amplitudeencoding","identifier":"doc:\/\/AmplitudeEncoding\/documentation\/AmplitudeEncoding","abstract":[{"text":"Send records to an Amplitude project through its HTTP V2 API.","type":"text"}],"role":"collection"},"doc://AmplitudeEncoding/documentation/AmplitudeEncoding/AmplitudeRegion":{"title":"AmplitudeRegion","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"AmplitudeRegion"}],"url":"\/documentation\/amplitudeencoding\/amplituderegion","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The data center an Amplitude project’s data resides in, which decides the HTTP V2 endpoint its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"events are posted to."}],"r